cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ghostmaxxing: a browser-side lab for testing face-recognition camouflage"
message: "If you use this software or reference it in research, please cite it."
type: software
version: 0.9.9
date-released: 2026-09-01
authors:
  - name: "Claudio Agosti (me.vecna.eu)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/vecna/ghostmaxxing"
url: "https://ghostmaxxing.vecna.eu/"
abstract: >-
  Ghostmaxxing is a static, client-side web application for testing
  face-recognition camouflage. A local recognition pipeline runs against a
  webcam feed in the browser; users enrol a baseline face, alter their
  appearance through painted overlays or plugin "Ghostyles", and observe the
  match response in real time. Results are local and conditional and are not
  claims of protection against any deployed system.
keywords:
  - facial recognition
  - adversarial makeup
  - anti-biometric
  - computer vision
  - CV Dazzle
  - web AR
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
